{
  "id": "kanizsa-figure",
  "term": "Kanizsa figure",
  "definition": "A Kanizsa figure is a visual pattern in which appropriately arranged openings in visible shapes, called inducers, make people perceive the edges and surface of a figure even though those contours are not physically drawn. In the example described, four circle segments can create the impression of an illusory rectangle.",
